---
description: Python style for Astraq ML service
globs: services/ml/**/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

# Typing
- All public functions fully typed. `from __future__ import annotations` in every module.
- No `Any` without a comment explaining why.

# Structure
- Keep routers thin and move business logic into services or domain modules.
- Keep config and environment handling centralized.

# Errors
- Raise `HTTPException` only at the HTTP layer. Internal code should raise domain errors.

# Time-series safety
- Feature at time `t` may only use data with timestamp `< t`.
- Use time-aware validation such as walk-forward splits for forecasting and strategy work.
- No `shuffle=True` on time series.
- Report out-of-sample metrics and compare against a simple baseline when it makes sense.

# Config
- Use `pydantic-settings`. Fail fast on missing env. No `os.environ.get` scattered in code.
